Z||000025||p4n1c||05-31-2001||03:45 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by kslish:<BR><B>I've noticed that single women tend to have their "guy friends" and then they usually have their "a**hole boyfriend."  It seems that women are much better at defining (in their minds at least) the difference between "friends" and "love interest" while guys always seem to be testing the boundries of friendship to take it one step further...or interpreting what is really only a friendship with a girl as being something else (I've made this mistake many a time before).  Maybe a female on this board can validate these ideas that I have....okay off the soapbox now.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Interesting insight and I've had the same observation, they always seem to be able to pick the a$$hole to be their boyfriend and think their guy friends are to nice and will find someone sometime.  <P>You might be right about the friend thing, I never thought of that.  Oh well, we'll see what happens.  I'm not going to worry about it.  Life goes on.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  It seems the hardest for nice guys(well I think I'm a nice guy anyway) to meet women.  Especially in this city.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><P>------------------<BR>-=-=-=[ p4n1c ]=-=-=-<BR>1988 Olds Cutlass Supreme International<BR>2.8L MPFI V6/TH440-T4 OD auto<BR>"Ride the geriatric mobile.. err..  rocket"<p>[This message has been edited by p4n1c (edited 05-31-2001).]||||reg||1
