Z||000029||grinthock||05-31-2001||05:25 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroLisa:<BR><B>Well good that I'm the first female to respond to this    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>The answer: hell, I don't know, every girl has her own motives.  We don't even know what we want, except to be liked (usually) and to get attention (usually)<P>So while we're at it, Why do guys always show up late or completely forget about dates? Why do they ask a girl out with only the intentions of getting her in bed? Uggg...men....<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I am gonna take a shot in the dark here at the risk of getting my a$$ kicked, car bombed, or head kicked.... hehehe.. (84bill do'nt even TRY to join in!)<P>At least Lisa is able to admit that she wants attention.. That's good, all women want it and that's a trust statement, attention makes them happy about themselves because in today's society women get the feeling that if they are not whisled at they are un-attractive (I hear that jive alot from friends)<P>Lisa.... We do'nt always forget, infact I am never late for a date, If I think there is a chance I might get late I always give the notice at date agreement time, ie "I am working till 5, but sometimes I am asked to work later so I may need to be later, if so, I will call as soon as I know, is this OK with you?"<P>As for the sex thing, I gotta admit, there are people who go for just that, they brag about nailing some chick on the first date, honestly.  I just can't do it on the first date, I need to know the person otherwise it's mindless, mindless sex is lust not sex.   I guess as we get older we just learn to appriciate sex with that special someone.... Lisa, do'nt fret we don't ALL do that.  As for understanding womens feelings/emotions or otherwise?  I gave up YEARS ago, when my Fiancee freaks out over something I say, or do, or comes home crying and I ask what's worng and she just shakes her head and won't talk, I just accept it as part of how women work.<P>NOW -- As for the topic at hand, I don't think women lead men.  Women are so encouraged by the media these days to "Work it" and make themselves look great, so some guys thinks WOW, she is showing cleavage she must want sex, or some chick hugs you during a date that means sex... Nope, it's her warming up to you a bit... YES some women do do it, I know women who do it for FUN!  And they enjoy leading then dropping guys.. it's mean... it's cruel... guys do it too.. but I think women do it more... <P>that's my 45 cents.||||reg||1
