Z||000049||Mach10||06-03-2001||07:56 PM||||Been in a steady, stable relationship for over 3 years. I love this Girl!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P>She's everything I could ever need, or want.<P>The "Ultimate" rejection? by a Lesbian? Nah. That's just life. This is the ultimate rejection:<P>Was good friends with this girl for years. Then we started hanging out on a more social basis for a while. Took a while, but I made it fairly clear that I was interested, and she reciprocated. I was somewhat shy, so never actually got up to asking her out on a <B>date</B> date. Finally did, and she agreed readily. Made arrangements to go see a movie. Said, "Sure, but I might be stuck with the family. Will call you." Sure enough, got the call. Family off to the lake. No biggie, reschedule. Same sort of thing for a couple of weeks, decided that she might be avoiding the issue, so I backed off. Continued the social thing, seemed to be hitting off great. After another year of this, with PLENTY of body-language to suggest things were going in  a positive direction (won't bore you w. details  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">) I mustered the courage to try again, and met with the same thing 4 times. I finally just broke down and asked if she truly wanted anything to do with me. The answer was, obviously "No". 2 years of leading me on... So then, me, being the valiant gent I was suggested then that we just continue as friends and forget this whole thing (she was a blast to hang out with). That's when she said: "No, I don't think we can do that either, because it's something of a falsity on my part."<BR>I remember that clearly, and still want to pimp-slap her and kill her pets  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P>That's the ultimate rejection.||||reg||1
Z||000050||p4n1c||06-04-2001||10:01 AM||||Holy sh1t man.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">  My rejection is pale in comparison to that.||||reg||1
Z||000051||JSocha||06-04-2001||10:18 AM||||Sometimes, I just think women don't know what they want either.<P>Like this line they typically give you "I just want to remain friends" and/or "I don't want to ruin our friendship...", even if you have been sleepin with em for months and would like to consider yourself BF/GF or would like to take what you feel is a growing relationship to possibliy the next level and to which they do not and to which they wanted to sleep with you and initiated the sexual relationship in the first place.<P>That would be equivelant if one of us guys had responded after she indicated she wants to get married to yah with the statement "I don't want to ruin our friendship...".<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000052||FieroLisa||06-04-2001||10:44 AM||||grinthock...I think you're insulting me, but I'm gonna ignore it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>It's not necessarily that we don't know what we want, but here's an example. I meet a guy, he seems nice, attractive, blah blah, whatever, we go out. Then I really figure the guy out and realize he's a jackass that I can't connect with, so even though it seems that I have been leading him on for 2 weeks, its really that I've realized that even though initially he seemed like a prospective, now I know we just don't click.<P>And then it's like your in this relationship and you feel BAD for dumping the guy so you procrastinate and try to find the *nicest* way until one day you can't handle it anymore and it just kinda comes out b*tchy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000053||p4n1c||06-04-2001||10:55 AM||||I hope she didn't think I was a jackass, I may be a little wierd and shy, but I'm not a jackass.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Ah well, the world hasn't ended, so I think I'm okay for now.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>-=-=-=[ p4n1c ]=-=-=-<BR>1988 Olds Cutlass Supreme International<BR>2.8L MPFI V6/TH440-T4 OD auto<BR>"Ride the geriatric mobile.. err..  rocket"||||reg||1
Z||000054||Fierochic88||06-04-2001||11:03 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><P>And then it's like your in this relationship and you feel BAD for dumping the guy so you procrastinate and try to find the *nicest* way until one day you can't handle it anymore and it just kinda comes out b*tchy   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">[/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I know exactly how you feel :-)<P><BR>Jennifer<BR><P>------------------<BR>Silver 1988 GT<BR>Silver 1986 2m4<P>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/ViewPhoto?u=34301&a=798574&p=12690689&f=0||||reg||1
Z||000055||Ken Wittlief||06-04-2001||11:19 AM||||The hardest thing with relationships is that when you first meet someone you know almost nothing about them.<P>  but you have in the back of your mind what you would LIKE them to be, you have an idea of what they SHOULD be like.<P>  so you start getting to know each other, and over time your perception of the other person is replaced by the reality of what they are really like.<P>   usually they are very different from what you want, and you end up breaking it off.<P>  When a person has high expectations of what they want in a mate, its impossible for anyone to live up to their preconceived notions. <P>   The funny part of all this is we all do it, and we dont realize we are doing it - not only with relationships, with everything - jobs, cars, careers, houses, hobbies, vacations...<P>   its impossible for us to know everything about everything, so we fill in the blanks with what WE THINK things and people should be like.<P>  then we are dissapointed when the real world is not like that. Then we go further and say, "Its not fair! - its not suppose to be like this!"<P>   the funniest part of this, is when someone else really gets to know you, and then they tell you, 'you really changed - you use to be different'<P>   when in fact you havent changed at all, they are only compairing the real you to what they thought you would be like.||||reg||1
Z||000056||FieroLisa||06-04-2001||01:09 PM||||ah yes, the old "you used to be different" line.... <P>||||reg||1
Z||000057||p4n1c||06-04-2001||02:16 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><B>then we are dissapointed when the real world is not like that. Then we go further and say, "Its not fair! - its not suppose to be like this!"</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I usually don't say that, it's usually, "Sh1t happens" or "C'est la vie".  I guess you get used to unfair crap happening to you after a few years.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><B>the funniest part of this, is when someone else really gets to know you, and then they tell you, 'you really changed - you use to be different'</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>This is so true, I heard this less than 2 months ago when I broke up with my then girlfriend.  I seem to be the same, sure I've grown up a little, but that isn't much of a change that is linked to a statement like that.<P>------------------<BR>-=-=-=[ p4n1c ]=-=-=-<BR>1988 Olds Cutlass Supreme International<BR>2.8L MPFI V6/TH440-T4 OD auto<BR>"Ride the geriatric mobile.. err..  rocket"||||reg||1
Z||000058||Ken Wittlief||06-04-2001||02:49 PM||||Its more than that. Some people wander out into the real world, thinking it will be the way THEY think it should be<P>and when its different<P>instead of adjusting their mental model of the world<P>they keep running the old model, the one they made up<P>and then they get mad at the world for not being "The way its suppose to be!"<P>who says how its suppose to be?!<P>You? them? God? <P>this may seem like a subtle point, but some people get so stuck on "its not fair - its not right" they never learn to deal with the world the way it is.<P>engineers call it feedback - you test the waters, see what happens and then you adjust YOUR actions accordingly.<P> the people that dont adjust go through life angry, waiting for the world to change to suit them.<P>and nothing changes, and their life is the same and never gets better.||||reg||1
